{
  "requirement": "`ValidationCache::new()` creates an empty cache for running criteria without\nan agent.\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl<D: Domain> ValidationCache<D> {\n    pub fn new() -> Self;\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "structural: The structural obligation is the prescribed signature: `impl<D: Domain> ValidationCache<D> { pub fn new() -> Self; }`. `crates/trust-but-verify/src/domain.rs#impl[ValidationCache<D>]/fn[new]` is declared in that impl block with the same signature. It returns `Self::default()`. The `Default` impl at `impl[ValidationCache<D>/Default]` makes every shared collection empty and leaves `sources` and `agent` as `None`. That gives an empty cache with no agent, as the requirement states.\n\nThe delegation to `Default` is a discretionary choice. The text does not require it. A `new` that built the fields directly would behave the same and still meet the text. The signature is the only structural clause, and the single root covers it. The phrases \"empty cache\" and \"without an agent\" describe observable behavior, so they create no further structural obligation.\n\nbehavioral: `requirements.sdk.validation-cache.new` has two obligations. `ValidationCache::new()` must create an empty cache. That cache must be usable for running criteria without an agent.\n\n- **Empty cache without an agent:** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[new_cache_starts_without_files_or_agent]` calls `ValidationCache::<TestDomain>::new()`. It asserts that `agent` is `None`, that `sources` is `None`, and that `outlines` is empty. These are the externally meaningful state fields: the agent configuration, the source set, and the cached files. The struct also has `usage`, `nodes` and `source_addresses` fields. The test does not assert them, and I did not treat that as a gap. The requirement names no observable obligation for them beyond the cache being empty.\n- **Usable without an agent:** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_clones_share_the_first_successful_outline_for_each_path]` creates a cache with `ValidationCache::<Application>::new()`. It then uses that cache to produce and share outlines, with no agent configured. This shows the new cache works for outline-based criteria. It is also marked `{test}` for this requirement.\n\nBoth tests carry `{test}` markers and have real assertions. I found no gap.",
