        "status": "success",
        "rationale": "The structural obligation is the prescribed signature: `impl<D: Domain> ValidationCache<D> { pub fn new() -> Self; }`. `crates/trust-but-verify/src/domain.rs#impl[ValidationCache<D>]/fn[new]` is declared in that impl block with the same signature. It returns `Self::default()`. The `Default` impl at `impl[ValidationCache<D>/Default]` makes every shared collection empty and leaves `sources` and `agent` as `None`. That gives an empty cache with no agent, as the requirement states.\n\nThe delegation to `Default` is a discretionary choice. The text does not require it. A `new` that built the fields directly would behave the same and still meet the text. The signature is the only structural clause, and the single root covers it. The phrases \"empty cache\" and \"without an agent\" describe observable behavior, so they create no further structural obligation."
      }
