        "status": "success",
        "rationale": "`requirements.sdk.validation-cache.new` has two obligations. `ValidationCache::new()` must create an empty cache. That cache must be usable for running criteria without an agent.\n\n- **Empty cache without an agent:** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[new_cache_starts_without_files_or_agent]` calls `ValidationCache::<TestDomain>::new()`. It asserts that `agent` is `None`, that `sources` is `None`, and that `outlines` is empty. These are the externally meaningful state fields: the agent configuration, the source set, and the cached files. The struct also has `usage`, `nodes` and `source_addresses` fields. The test does not assert them, and I did not treat that as a gap. The requirement names no observable obligation for them beyond the cache being empty.\n- **Usable without an agent:** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_clones_share_the_first_successful_outline_for_each_path]` creates a cache with `ValidationCache::<Application>::new()`. It then uses that cache to produce and share outlines, with no agent configured. This shows the new cache works for outline-based criteria. It is also marked `{test}` for this requirement.\n\nBoth tests carry `{test}` markers and have real assertions. I found no gap."
